# EVERY MARKDOWN FILE. The docs are mostly WIDE TABLES (the README's Usage
# table, the router's labs and areas, the skills), and Prettier re-pads every
# row of a table whenever a single cell changes width — so a one-row edit
# arrives as a diff over the whole table, the actual change is invisible in
# review, and two branches that each touch one row conflict over all of them.
# Markdown is written by hand and kept as written: compact `| a | b |`
# tables, and the line breaks the author meant. (This also covers
# CHANGELOG.md, machine-written by the release workflow, and OSS_GAME_SPEC.md,
# a verbatim copy.)
*.md
# The agent router's symlinked aliases, named one by one: Prettier resolves a
# symlink before matching this list, and the ones without an `.md` name are
# not caught by the line above (`tests/symlinks_test.ts` holds the list).
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# The agent skills and the lesson fragments beside them (`.claude/skills` and
# `.gemini/skills` are symlinks onto the same tree) — whatever is in them,
# Markdown or not, is written by whichever session is doing that subject's
# work, and parallel sessions must never meet over a re-formatted block.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/
.gemini/skills/
